      },
      "parts": [
        {
          "type": "step-start",
          "id": "prt_0f73d917d001ANy8KS1uS7hcot",
          "sessionID": "ses_f08c2967effeRJDzMKrrYrxRRI",
          "messageID": "msg_0f73d8748001Q0zABO9rnng7kZ"
        },
        {
          "type": "reasoning",
          "text": "Let me analyze the implementation:\n\n```python\ndef overlaps(left, right):\n    \"\"\"Return whether two intervals share an integer point.\"\"\"\n    return max(left[0], right[0]) <= min(left[1], right[1])\n```\n\nFor half-open intervals [start, end), the standard overlap test is:\n- overlap iff max(left[0], right[0]) < min(left[1], right[1])\n\nThe current code uses `<=`, which incorrectly reports that:\n- Touching intervals overlap: [1, 2) and [2, 3): max(1,2)=2, min(2,3)=2, 2<=2 → True, but they only touch at point 2 which is excluded from the first interval and not included in either shared point. Actually [1,2) contains 1; [2,3) contains 2. They share no integer point. So should be False.\n- Empty intervals overlap: [2, 2) and [2, 5): max(2,2)=2, min(2,5)=2, 2<=2 → True, but empty interval contains no points, so should be False. Also [3,3) and [1,3): max(3,1)=3, min(3,3)=3 → True but should be False.\n\nThe fix: change `<=` to `<`.\n\nCheck genuinely overlapping: [1,4) and [2,5): max(1,2)=2 < min(4,5)=4 → True. Good.\n\nDisjoint: [1,2) and [5,6): max(1,5)=5 < min(2,6)=2 → False. Good.\n\nNow apply the fix with replace.",
          "time": {
            "start": 1790854402432,
            "end": 1790854407417
          },
          "id": "prt_0f73d9180001vDD9mRV3zwnLtF",
          "sessionID": "ses_f08c2967effeRJDzMKrrYrxRRI",
          "messageID": "msg_0f73d8748001Q0zABO9rnng7kZ"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The implementation is found. The bug is in `overlaps`: it uses `<=`, which makes touching intervals like `[1,2)` and `[2,3)` (sharing no integer point, since 2 is excluded from the first) and empty intervals like `[2,2)` report as overlapping. For half-open intervals the shared-point test must be strict: `max(starts) < min(ends)`.\n\n{\"action\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"intervals.py\",\"old\":\"    return max(left[0], right[0]) <= min(left[1], right[1])\",\"new\":\"    return max(left[0], right[0]) < min(left[1], right[1])\"}",
          "time": {
            "start": 1790854407419,
            "end": 1790854409005
          },
          "id": "prt_0f73da4fb001odbmbdwFTJNJIS",
          "sessionID": "ses_f08c2967effeRJDzMKrrYrxRRI",
          "messageID": "msg_0f73d8748001Q0zABO9rnng7kZ"
        },
